Not every workload has identical technical or business requirements. Classifying workloads before deployment helps determine the appropriate Azure services, security controls, and availability requirements.

Common workload categories include:

* Business-critical
* Mission-critical
* Development and testing
* Batch processing
* Analytics
* Web applications
* Disaster recovery

For example, an internal HR portal may tolerate short maintenance windows, whereas an online payment gateway requires continuous availability and strict security controls.

A real-life use case is organisations allocating different service levels and budgets according to workload importance rather than treating every application equally.

Proper workload classification improves architecture decisions and operational planning.
